{
 "duration": 55.95,
 "captions": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "text": "Don't run your generator in the garage.",
   "end": 2.28
  },
  {
   "start": 2.28,
   "text": "Not even with the door open.",
   "end": 4.07
  },
  {
   "start": 4.07,
   "text": "This is the mistake that kills people on day two of a blackout.",
   "end": 7.78
  },
  {
   "start": 7.78,
   "text": "Day two. The freezer is giving up, the house is cold, so people get careful.",
   "end": 12.77
  },
  {
   "start": 12.77,
   "text": "They don't run it inside the house.",
   "end": 14.68
  },
  {
   "start": 14.68,
   "text": "They put it in the garage...",
   "end": 15.89
  },
  {
   "start": 15.89,
   "text": "and crack the door.",
   "end": 17.24
  },
  {
   "start": 17.24,
   "text": "And here's why that still kills.",
   "end": 19.32
  },
  {
   "start": 19.32,
   "text": "Carbon monoxide has no smell.",
   "end": 21.49
  },
  {
   "start": 21.49,
   "text": "No color. It doesn't make you cough.",
   "end": 23.66
  },
  {
   "start": 23.66,
   "text": "It drifts from the garage into the house.",
   "end": 26.1
  },
  {
   "start": 26.1,
   "text": "The first signs are a headache...",
   "end": 27.86
  },
  {
   "start": 27.86,
   "text": "dizziness... feeling tired.",
   "end": 29.85
  },
  {
   "start": 29.85,
   "text": "In the dark, on day two, that feels normal.",
   "end": 32.74
  },
  {
   "start": 32.74,
   "text": "So people lie down.",
   "end": 34.11
  },
  {
   "start": 34.11,
   "text": "The CDC counts more than four hundred deaths a year in the US from carbon monoxide that has nothing to do with fires.",
   "end": 40.45
  },
  {
   "start": 40.45,
   "text": "And it says: don't even run a car in an attached garage with the door open.",
   "end": 45.03
  },
  {
   "start": 45.03,
   "text": "The rule: generators, grills and camp stoves go outside.",
   "end": 48.99
  },
  {
   "start": 48.99,
   "text": "At least twenty feet from doors and windows.",
   "end": 51.39
  },
  {
   "start": 51.39,
   "text": "And put a battery-powered CO alarm in your home.",
   "end": 54.05
  },
  {
   "start": 54.05,
   "text": "It's the only thing that will warn you.",
   "end": 55.95
  }
 ],
